of an element."}],"kind":"symbol","type":"topic"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLOtherNotation":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The other-notation type is used to define any notations not yet in the MusicXML format. It handles notations"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"where more specific extension elements such as other-dynamics and other-technical are not appropriate. The"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"smufl attribute can be used to specify a particular notation, allowing application interoperability without"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"requiring every SMuFL glyph to have a MusicXML element equivalent. Using the other-notation type without the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"smufl attribute allows for extended representation, though without application interoperability."}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlothernotation","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLOtherNotation","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","title":"MXLOtherNotation","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MXLOtherNotation","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLOtherNotation","role":"symbol"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL":{"type":"topic","title":"IvorMXL","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A MusicXML parser, normalizer, validator, and formatter."}],"role":"collection","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLColor":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The color type indicates the color of an element. Color may be represented as hexadecimal RGB triples, as in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"HTML, or as hexadecimal ARGB tuples, with the A indicating alpha of transparency. An alpha value of 00 is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"totally transparent; FF is totally opaque. If RGB is used, the A value is assumed to be FF."}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlcolor","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLColor"}],"kind":"symbol","title":"MXLColor","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLColor"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLColor","role":"symbol"}}}